00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.020
This year started off with an unequivocal bang with Madhouse's release of "Death Parade"

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:40.560
The show that managed to trick the entire anime community into falling into an existential crisis, while they were busy putting their hands up to funk.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.160
The anime asks the question of how a person acts when pushed their mental limits

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.440
and does this by forcing two characters to play a game against each other with their lives on the line.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:55.280
What the characters don't know is that they are actually in the afterlife, and their actions during this game will decide whether they are sent to either Heaven or Hell.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.540
It was an interesting premise that managed to explore all different directions of your moral compass without ever being too preachy

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.300
and it's one of the few shows that allows you to reflect on your own life.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:10.160
Are you satisfied with it? Or is there an undercurrent of dismay just slowly realizing the insignificance of your own existence

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:15.760
Traveling towards an unavoidable death as you're trapped living the 9 to 5 grind with no escape...

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:16.780
